I added four patterns to the Reelbox (ott) variant and wrote `trickster-output.json`. Typecheck and build both pass. I did not run the Playwright tests or the gates, so the happy-path driver and the `verify` rules are unchecked.

- **p1, Playback assurance (`basket_sneaking`, signup-plan):** a ₹57.82 line (₹49 plus GST) is included by default. It has a neutral label and no checkbox. The only control is a tiny "Remove" button in the "Due today" breakdown. The honest total of ₹531 becomes ₹588.82.
- **p2, partner sharing (`interface_interference`, signup-plan):** a switch-style button that reads "Partner sharing: On" and shares viewing activity with partners. The shopper has to switch it off.
- **p3, UPI check on cheap plans (`forced_action`, signup-plan, `offPath`):** for Mobile and Basic, a "couldn't confirm your UPI" panel blocks "Continue to payment". The primary button switches the shopper to Standard. "Try again" is a link and clears the block on the first click. Standard and Premium never see the panel.
- **p4, retention offer (`subscription_trap`, cancel flow):** the cancel screen leads with a large "Claim 50% off" card. The copy states a new 3-month term that renews at full price. The real "Cancel membership" button (`account.cancel.confirm`) is now a link variant at the bottom of the screen, but it is still on screen for the driver.

The existing extra-member add-on stays as decoy d1. There are three tasks, covering the Standard plan, the cheapest phone plan and cance
